From 38c2b1c1a2de3d9b781b504fb3fbbf76c22a373b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: obi nwosu <obinwosu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:39:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hdPhantom: warm up the HID Touch before opening it

With the HID Geomagic Touch (USB 2988:0304) and the Sep 2024 Touch
driver, about half of the first hdInitDevice() calls in a process leave
the motors off. Nothing reports it: force output reads on, calibration
OK, no HD error. Whether the motors come on follows a repeatable
sequence over the open count, and from about the 21st open in a process
they always do. The simulator opens the drill once, so each launch was
a coin flip: no force until it was restarted.

Do 20 quick hdInitDevice/hdDisableDevice cycles (no servo loop, no
force, ~1.2 s) before the real open. Measured by pulsing a resting
stylus and reading the encoders: 20/20 with the warm-up vs 0/10
without it through this library, 50/50 loaded the way the simulator
loads it, plus working force in a real simulator launch.

FIVRS_HAPTIC_WARMUP=0 turns it off; another number sets the cycle
count. It stops early if no device opens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../chai3d/extras/hdPhantom/hdPhantom.cpp     | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/external/chai3d/extras/hdPhantom/hdPhantom.cpp b/core/external/chai3d/extras/hdPhantom/hdPhantom.cpp
index 4f1299a2..2098f232 100644
--- a/core/external/chai3d/extras/hdPhantom/hdPhantom.cpp
+++ b/core/external/chai3d/extras/hdPhantom/hdPhantom.cpp
@@ -185,6 +185,30 @@ _hdLoad(void)
         HDErrorInfo error;
         numPhantomDevices = 0;
 
+        // Warm-up for the HID Touch (USB 2988:0304) with the Sep 2024 driver:
+        // on about half of the first opens in a process the motors stay off,
+        // with no error reported (force output on, calibration OK). From
+        // about the 21st open on they always come on. 20 quick open/close
+        // cycles first (~1.2 s, no servo loop, no force) made every following
+        // open work: 80/80 vs 14/30 without (2026-11-14, see
+        // ~/haptic_setup/diag/pulse_warmup.txt). FIVRS_HAPTIC_WARMUP=0 turns
+        // it off; any other number sets the cycle count.
+        {
+            int warmup = 20;
+            const char* env = getenv("FIVRS_HAPTIC_WARMUP");
+            if (env) warmup = atoi(env);
+            for (int i = 0; i < warmup; i++)
+            {
+                HHD hWarm = hdInitDevice(HD_DEFAULT_DEVICE);
+                if (HD_DEVICE_ERROR(hdGetError()) || hWarm == HD_INVALID_HANDLE)
+                {
+                    while (HD_DEVICE_ERROR(hdGetError())) {}
+                    break;   // no device: stop warming up
+                }
+                hdDisableDevice(hWarm);
+            }
+        }
+
         // search for a first device
         HHD hHD0 = hdInitDevice(HD_DEFAULT_DEVICE);
 
